"""Reference-as-solution wrapper for FlagGems ``sigmoid_backward``.

Injected through the existing formal override path only:

    --override sigmoid_backward:<this file>:run

It imports no ``flag_gems`` symbol and never calls the export it replaces
(``flag_gems.sigmoid_backward``), so it cannot use the candidate as its own
oracle and cannot re-enter the injected wrapper.

Two callsites exist for this operator in the frozen suites, and this file
follows both of them instead of inventing an ABI:

1. Correctness callsite (``tests/test_sigmoid.py::test_sigmoid_backward``,
   the frozen master body): ``flag_gems.sigmoid_backward(res_grad, res_out)``
   with the oracle ``torch.ops.aten.sigmoid_backward(ref_grad, ref_out)``.
   That call is made *outside* any ``flag_gems.use_gems()`` scope, and the
   override only rebinds the ``flag_gems`` module attribute
   (``dynamic_registry.DynamicOpOverride.override`` is a plain ``setattr``),
   so ``torch.ops.aten.sigmoid_backward`` here stays the native ATen op and is
   therefore safe to delegate to. It preserves the frozen contract that the
   test asserts: same dtype/device/shape as the input, one fresh output tensor,
   no input mutation.

2. Benchmark callsite (``benchmark/test_sigmoid.py::test_sigmoid_backward``):
   ``base.UnaryPointwiseBenchmark(op_name="sigmoid_backward",
   torch_op=torch.sigmoid, is_backward=True)`` builds a *single* input tensor
   and calls the timed callable as ``op(x)`` before differentiating it
   (``benchmark/base.py`` ``UnaryPointwiseBenchmark.get_input_iter`` /
   ``Benchmark._benchmark_callable``, ``torch.autograd.grad``). The unary arm
   below therefore returns the benchmark's own declared forward
   ``torch.sigmoid(x)``; its backward step is ``aten::sigmoid_backward``, i.e.
   the timed quantity is the same sigmoid-backward kernel the frozen native
   baseline (``self.torch_op``) times. A two-argument-only wrapper would raise
   ``TypeError`` inside the timing loop, so this single unary arm is the
   harness ABI, not a second operator.
"""

import torch

_UNSET = object()


def run(grad_output, output=_UNSET):
    """sigmoid_backward reference solution.

    ``run(grad_output, output)``: native ``aten::sigmoid_backward`` oracle.
    ``run(x)``: benchmark harness ABI, returns ``torch.sigmoid(x)``.
    """
    if output is _UNSET:
        return torch.sigmoid(grad_output)
    return torch.ops.aten.sigmoid_backward(grad_output, output)
